# Interface contract (AGENT-PROPOSED, not student-approved)

Authoritative declarations: `platform/capstone_bridge.h` (version 1).

## Ownership
| File | Owner |
|---|---|
| platform/doomgeneric_wasm.c (DG_* adapters, main), platform/capstone_bridge.h, web/index.html, Makefile, BUILD.md | coder |
| platform/render_timing.{c,h}, web/render_timing.js | coder_render_timing |
| platform/input_audio.{c,h}, web/input_audio.js | coder_input_audio |
| tests/ | tester |

## DG adapter mapping (coder implements; specialists supply the cap_* side)
| Engine callback | Forwards to |
|---|---|
| DG_Init | cap_render_init(); cap_input_init(); cap_audio_init() |
| DG_DrawFrame | cap_render_present(DG_ScreenBuffer) |
| DG_SleepMs | cap_sleep_ms |
| DG_GetTicksMs | cap_time_ms |
| DG_GetKey | cap_input_poll |
| DG_SetWindowTitle | cap_set_title |

## Engine facts the modules rely on (verified in source)
- DG_ScreenBuffer is malloc'd inside doomgeneric_Create before DG_Init; 640x400x4.
- Pixel bytes in memory: B,G,R,0. Alpha is 0 -> must be forced to 255.
- I_GetTime() uses basetime==0 as "unset"; DG_GetTicksMs must be nonzero on
  first call or the time base re-latches.
- Blocking waits exist: d_main.c wipe loop (`do { I_GetTime(); I_Sleep(1); }
  while (tics<=0)`) and d_loop.c TryRunTics (`I_Sleep(1)` until a tic elapses).
  cap_sleep_ms must therefore not busy-hang: it may spin on the real clock for
  <= ~1-2 ms or yield via Asyncify/ASYNCIFY_SLEEP; the render_timing owner picks
  the mechanism and tells coder the needed flags (e.g. -sASYNCIFY). Real time
  MUST advance during these waits.
- DG_GetKey: key codes are already Doom codes (TranslateKey is identity); see
  doomkeys.h. I_GetEvent stops after the first release event per call, so the
  queue must tolerate being polled repeatedly. Return 0 when empty.
- Shift state is tracked from KEY_RSHIFT events only.

## Control flow
1. main(): mount/preload WAD, call doomgeneric_Create(argc, argv) with
   argv = {"doom","-iwad","/doom1.wad"} (add "-nosound"-equivalent not needed;
   FEATURE_SOUND is off by default).
2. Browser drives `cap_frame()` per animation frame (emscripten_set_main_loop
   or JS rAF); each call is one doomgeneric_Tick(), presenting via DG_DrawFrame.
3. JS -> C input only via cap_input_event / cap_input_reset (browser events are
   queued, never call engine directly).

## Build interface (coder)
`make clean`, `make all` -> dist/index.html, doom.js, doom.wasm, doom.data.
Sources: third_party/doomgeneric/*.c excluding platform-specific/unneeded
(dummy.c handling, i_cdmus, i_joystick, net_* to be confirmed at build time),
plus platform/*.c, with `-I third_party/doomgeneric -I platform`. Specialists
request flags/files from coder through their report.md; coder integrates.

## Open items / change process
Contract changes: specialist describes the exact change in report.md; coder
bumps CAP_BRIDGE_VERSION and updates this file in a later attempt.
Audio (DG_sound_module/DG_music_module, SDL_mixer include in i_sound.c) is
UNDECIDED scope; `cap_audio_init` is a placeholder only.
# Proposed specification (AGENT-PROPOSED, not student-approved)

Source: commit e500c44 + uncommitted loop/ changes. No student-authored
artifacts/specification.md existed at planning time; this is a fallback.

## Scope
- Port supplied doomgeneric (C) to WebAssembly with Emscripten 4.0.18 (pinned
  per README/Dockerfile). Browser target: Chromium (current stable).
- Use only assets/doom1.wad (shareware Episode 1), packaged into the module
  (`--preload-file`) at `/doom1.wad`; launched with `-iwad /doom1.wad`.
- Output: dist/{index.html,doom.js,doom.wasm,doom.data}; served from a local
  static server (`python3 -m http.server --directory dist`).
- Build: root `Makefile` with `clean` and `all`; documented in BUILD.md.

## Functional requirements (proposed)
- R1 Boot: page loads with no console errors; title screen/menu appear.
- R2 Display: 640x400 canvas, correct colors (B,G,R,0 -> opaque RGBA), no
  tearing or channel swap.
- R3 Timing: engine runs at ~35 tics/s of real time; main loop yields to the
  browser every frame (requestAnimationFrame / emscripten main loop); screen
  melt wipe and tic-sync waits do not freeze the tab.
- R4 Input: keyboard only. Arrows move/turn, Ctrl fire, Space use, Shift run,
  Alt/comma/period strafe, Enter/Esc/menu navigation, digits weapon select,
  Tab automap, Y/N prompts. Key release is delivered; focus loss releases keys.
- R5 Gameplay: New Game -> E1M1 reachable via menu; player can move, shoot,
  open doors, take damage, and progress state changes visibly.
- R6 Robustness: no crash/abort in a >= 5 minute scripted session.

## Explicitly UNDECIDED (student decision needed; not claimed done)
- Audio (SFX via Web Audio, music synthesis): not in default scope.
- Save/config persistence across reload (IDBFS).
- Mouse input (engine mouse events are commented out in i_input.c).
- Browsers other than Chromium; mobile/touch; deployment hosting headers.
- "Faithful play" definition beyond R1-R6 (e.g., demo/determinism checks).
Faithful-play acceptance MUST NOT be reported complete while these remain open.

## Assumptions
- emcc is not installed on this host (`which emcc` -> not found); Docker or
  emsdk 4.0.18 is needed before any build. Planning did not require it.
- tests/verify.sh (tester-owned) runs `make clean; make all; node
  tests/playtest.mjs`, with a hard-coded absolute cd path; neither Makefile
  nor playtest.mjs exists yet. Reported as a finding, not edited.
- Single-threaded build (no SharedArrayBuffer), so no COOP/COEP headers.
- Engine startup: doomgeneric_Create() runs D_DoomMain, which ends by calling
  doomgeneric_Tick() once and returns; so main() calls Create once then
  drives doomgeneric_Tick per frame.
# Proposed acceptance criteria (AGENT-PROPOSED by tester; NOT student-approved)

Basis: README.md, coder's proposed-spec.md (R1-R6) and interface-contract.md. No student
artifacts/acceptance-criteria.md existed. Student may replace/freeze these; until then they are provisional.
Implemented in `tests/playtest.mjs` (IDs match). Browser: Playwright Chromium 1.49.1 (131), viewport 800x600.

| ID | Criterion (observable) | Spec |
|---|---|---|
| B0 | `make clean && make all` succeeds from clean tree; dist/index.html + doom.wasm exist | build |
| B1 | `canvas#canvas` is 640x400 | R2 |
| B2 | Non-black frame with >16 colors within 60s of load | R1 |
| B3 | Canvas pixels opaque (alpha 255) | R2 |
| B4/B6 | Mean R >= mean B on title/menu and E1M1 (catches BGR swap) | R2 |
| B5 | No console errors, page errors, failed requests, or 404s | R1 |
| T1 | >=20 rAF/s over 3s (main loop yields) | R3 |
| M1 | Enter on title changes the display (menu opens) | R4/R5 |
| G1 | Enter x4 reaches a level: big change from menu and populated status bar | R5 |
| G2 | Idle frames stable (<2% pixels differ) | R5 |
| I1/I3 | Hold Right/Left turns the view: scene shifts >=8px in the correct direction | R4 |
| I2,I5,C3 | Motion/fire ceases after key release (<2% change over 0.5s) | R4 |
| I4/I6 | Forward changes view and keeps changing while held; Backward returns closer to start | R4 |
| I7 | Window blur while key held stops motion (no stuck key) | R4 |
| C1/C2 | Ctrl fire animates the view; ammo-counter region changes persistently | R5 |
| U1-U4 | Tab toggles automap and back; Esc opens/closes menu | R4 |
| R1-R4 | 300s scripted random-input soak: no errors/aborts, rAF >=20/s, last frame visible, frames changed, no longtask >=1.5s | R6 |
| selftest | Pixel helpers reject black / channel-swapped / transparent / static / mis-shifted frames | meta |

## Explicitly UNVERIFIED (reported every run; completion must not be claimed while open)
A1 audio (scope undecided; active AudioContext proves nothing), P1 save persistence, G3 door use /
level exit, T2 35 tics/s rate (needs a coder-provided tic counter hook; proposal: export `cap_tic_count()`).
Also not covered: other browsers, mouse, touch, "faithful play" vs. original (e.g. demo/determinism checks).

## Known weaknesses of these checks
Pixel heuristics can false-fail on legit layout variation (e.g., canvas scaled with different aspect/letterbox,
HUD region assumptions) and can false-pass on identical-looking wrong gameplay. Backward-return check depends on
E1M1 geometry. Soak input is seeded pseudo-random; the player may die, so soak proves stability, not progress.

## Assumptions
Page serves from dist/ via any static server (test uses its own, no special headers); canvas has id `canvas`;
default menu path is Enter x4 with defaults; keyboard bindings are the Doom defaults in proposed-spec R4.
